"""Optimized fused dequant-matmul Metal kernel for GGUF IQ3_XXS.

Replaces the scalar per-element inner loop of atf/gguf_metal.py for
IQ3_XXS with a llama.cpp-style vectorized loop:

  * one 32-lane SIMD-group per output element; each lane decodes WHOLE
    32-element sub-blocks per iteration (instead of striding K by 32
    with scalar byte loads),
  * block scale word S loaded once per sub-block (uint32 via 4 byte
    loads), four 7-bit sign fields unpacked once per sub-block,
  * activations loaded as float4 vectors,
  * codebook tables (ksigns[128] + iq3xxs grid uint32[256]) live in
    THREADGROUP memory, filled cooperatively at kernel start
    (NOTE: threadgroup uchar arrays misbehave under this MLX build --
    every threadgroup table is packed as uint words and unpacked
    with shifts),
  * qs indices read as two aligned ushort words per sub-block.

Numerics: bit-identical decode math to the validated scalar kernel;
only float accumulation order differs (relerr vs CPU reference
~2.3e-06 on the real 68 MB case tensor; tolerance 1e-3).

Wrapper matches gguf_matmul semantics:
    y[t, n] = sum_k x[t, k_base+k] * deq(row=n_base+n, col=k_base+k)
Requires k_base and k_len to be multiples of 32 (true for all MoE /
dense slices served by v11); asserts otherwise.
"""
